WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.535
This is Looks. Instead of a stack of settings,

00:00:07.535 --> 00:00:10.413
the panel starts with a few whole looks.

00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:13.814
Each look is drawn in the shape's own colors,

00:00:13.814 --> 00:00:16.607
with Stroke, Background and Edges right below.

00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:20.194
Those work just like today, one click each.

00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:24.974
The looks follow along in the new colors and edges,

00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:26.791
and the one that matches is marked.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:32.352
Now a whole look in one click: no fill, a thicker stroke and rougher lines.

00:00:35.012 --> 00:00:36.621
One undo puts it all back.

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:41.860
Cross-hatch keeps the green background and changes only the fill.

00:00:42.361 --> 00:00:44.776
Behind each color is the full picker,

00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:48.332
with the palette, shades and a hex code.

00:00:54.241 --> 00:00:58.801
The fine controls fold under More options:

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:04.228
Fill, Stroke width, Stroke style, Sloppiness and Opacity.

00:01:05.811 --> 00:01:09.074
Then Layers and Actions, like duplicate and delete.

00:01:14.495 --> 00:01:17.435
What works: you pick a result you can see,

00:01:17.435 --> 00:01:21.119
in your own colors, and one undo takes it back.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.788
The controls people change most stay right where they are.

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:29.144
What doesn't: six looks can't cover every mix,

00:01:29.144 --> 00:01:32.620
so some changes still mean opening More options.

00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:35.802
A look can also clear a background you set.

00:01:36.302 --> 00:01:39.982
And with More options open, the panel gets long and scrolls.
